; TitanProtocolEA.set
; Default input parameter template for mt5/TitanProtocolEA.mq5.
;
; This is a transport + execution bridge only -- it never generates,
; scores, or sizes trades. Replace ApiKey before attaching to any
; account; an empty key causes OnInit() to fail deliberately.
;
; ADR-034 Amendment 4: the EA's own compiled default for Transport is
; TRANSPORT_HTTP (WebRequest(), not native MQL5 socket) -- there is
; deliberately no Transport= line below, since this file's own
; personalization logic (install_mt5_files.py) cannot safely confirm
; MQL5's .set serialization format for a custom enum input without
; risking a silently-wrong value. Omitting it means MT5 applies the
; compiled default (Http) whenever this file is loaded. To opt into the
; native socket transport, set Transport=Socket explicitly in the EA's
; Inputs tab in MT5. SocketHost/SocketPort below are plain string/int
; inputs -- safe to personalize directly, and are filled in by
; install.py to match the live Bridge configuration's host/socket_port,
; ready for use the moment Transport=Socket is selected.

BackendUrl=http://127.0.0.1:8787
ApiKey=
HeartbeatIntervalSeconds=5
AllowedSymbolsCsv=
MagicNumber=20260710
MaxSlippagePoints=20
FailClosedTimeoutSeconds=30
EmergencyDisable=false
MaxRetries=3
RetryDelayMs=250
MaxRequoteRetries=2
RequoteRetryDelayMs=100
SocketHost=127.0.0.1
SocketPort=8788
SocketFailoverAfterAttempts=5
